  "corrections": {
    "audit_decision": "INSUFFICIENT_PUSCH_OPPORTUNITY",
    "correction_1": "Replace the 25000-byte/10-fps burst traffic with one fixed, lightweight, evenly paced 100-Hz/1200-byte UDP probe (~0.96 Mbps) that distributes ~10 independent PUSCH transmission opportunities across each 100-ms interval. This is measurement instrumentation, not SplitFusion application traffic or campaign throughput, and it is never tuned in response to a measurement outcome.",
    "correction_1_superseded_300mbps_note": "An earlier draft of this correction proposed reusing the capacity-study continuous 300-Mbps UDP iperf3 flow. That was superseded before any live execution by an explicit scientific amendment: RFsim controls the channel continuously, so saturating the scheduler is unnecessary and undesirable; only minimally invasive, evenly spaced transmission opportunities are needed. The 300-Mbps capacity evidence below is retained as historical provenance only and no longer gates the traffic design.",
    "correction_2": "Extend the causal observation window end from the nominal 100-ms tick to the actual next command's send time (or the clean-restoration command's send time for the final command in each profile), retaining the ACK+15ms guard start unchanged.",
    "original_gate_not_altered": true,
    "original_evidence_not_altered": true
  },
